{"about_the_game":"<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1816100/extras/31279e78a52bec0c9f3569a05247b386.avif?t=1737212280\" width=672 height=200 /></span><br><br><strong>Attention : VR Tablet PC supports keyboard input in English, Japanese and Korean.</strong><br><br><strong>What are you using a VR device for?</strong>        <strong>Just for fun? entertainment?</strong><br><br>Suppose you need to add a handwritten signature to an electronic document on a PC or <br>add a drawing by hand, and you only have a desktop PC and a mouse. <br><br>Besides, you don't have a tablet PC, pen type digitizer, camera, or scanner. <br><br>If so, do you have to buy them additionally? <br><br>If you have a VR device, you don't have to.   <br>You can use this app to perform the above actions in VR space.<br><br>Any PC-based app can be used in VR space, <br>so you can draw or write with any app you want.<br>And, edit it with another app. <br>And, attach an image, that has been edited, to another app to use.<br><strong>All of the above tasks can be batch-processed in VR space using VR Tablet PC.</strong><br><br><strong>If so, wouldn't that be a sufficient reason to use the VR device as a necessity?</strong><br><br><strong> If the work area cannot be seen well on the screen due to the limitation of resolution, <br>touch input work can be performed by enlarging only this part separately.</strong><br><br><strong> For Oculus users, it is recommended to use 'Touch Controller of Oculus Rift S' if possible.</strong>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/1816100?t=1737212280","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/1816100?t=1737212280","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1816100/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1737212280","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1816100/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1737212280","categories":[{"description":"Tracked Controller Support","id":52},{"description":"VR Only","id":54}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1816100/extras/31279e78a52bec0c9f3569a05247b386.avif?t=1737212280\" width=672 height=200 /></span><br><br><strong>Attention : VR Tablet PC supports keyboard input in English, Japanese and Korean.</strong><br><br><strong>What are you using a VR device for?</strong>        <strong>Just for fun? entertainment?</strong><br><br>Suppose you need to add a handwritten signature to an electronic document on a PC or <br>add a drawing by hand, and you only have a desktop PC and a mouse. <br><br>Besides, you don't have a tablet PC, pen type digitizer, camera, or scanner. <br><br>If so, do you have to buy them additionally? <br><br>If you have a VR device, you don't have to.   <br>You can use this app to perform the above actions in VR space.<br><br>Any PC-based app can be used in VR space, <br>so you can draw or write with any app you want.<br>And, edit it with another app. <br>And, attach an image, that has been edited, to another app to use.<br><strong>All of the above tasks can be batch-processed in VR space using VR Tablet PC.</strong><br><br><strong>If so, wouldn't that be a sufficient reason to use the VR device as a necessity?</strong><br><br><strong> If the work area cannot be seen well on the screen due to the limitation of resolution, <br>touch input work can be performed by enlarging only this part separately.</strong><br><br><strong> For Oculus users, it is recommended to use 'Touch Controller of Oculus Rift S' if possible.</strong>","developers":["Kim Yong Bum"],"genres":[{"description":"Design & Illustration","id":"53"},{"description":"Education","id":"54"},{"description":"Photo Editing","id":"55"},{"description":